## Approach

Replace the legacy snapshot aggregation (0–100 ad-hoc formula) with the new `scoring::score_file` system (1.0–10.0, category-capped). Store per-file and per-component health scores at each snapshot for historical drill-down. Rewrite the trend tool to diff at file/component/category granularity, plus a per-file history mode.

Key design choice: both new tables are **Ephemeral** (dropped on reindex, consistent with `snapshots` itself). File paths stored alongside file_ids so historical queries work within a session. SQLite dynamic typing lets us store f64 health_score in the existing INTEGER-affinity column without a schema migration for that field.

